bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27, 0, "Follow-up of interpreter_same_name_class_method_dispatch_collision_2026_11_26 (owner decision 2026-11-27: an alias names the owner-qualified class, so this must work). Two modules under src/compiler/70.backend/backend (zz_tmp_pa.spl / zz_tmp_pb.spl, copies of test/fixtures/same_name_class/pa.spl and pb.spl) each declare class Thing; a spec or run entry doing use compiler.backend.backend.zz_tmp_pa.{Thing} plus use compiler.backend.backend.zz_tmp_pb.{Thing as Legacy} fails on Thing.create() with: semantic: ambiguous type Thing: defined in .../zz_tmp_pa.spl, .../zz_tmp_pb.spl and none of them is imported by <entry> (module_cache.rs resolve_class_in_scope). Both braced imports load lazily and the entry owner has no recorded import bindings. Same on base f43f68c218e and on the fix. The identical import shape from test/fixtures/same_name_class resolves correctly (same_name_class_owner_identity_spec), so the gap is the entry-owner binding for these module paths. Loud error, not a wrong dispatch."

